Tab Start Values
Tab Start Values
Select the settings which determine how Plant Simulation interprets the time and the value column on the
tab Start Values.
Remarks
You can, for example, easily offset the data of a time sequence here.
The tab Start Values provides the settings listed in the table of contents to the left.
Set Value [TimeSequence]
11-4268 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Time Reference [TimeSequence]
Select if the time values are Relative or Absolute values.
Remarks
Depending on the setting you select, the data type of column 1 is time or dateTime. Plant Simulation
automatically converts values you specify.
• Absolute Time Reference
Type a point in time on a certain date (dateTime) into the text box Reference Date.
• Relative Time Reference
Type a duration (time) into the text box Reference Time.
SimTalk
Absolute [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
See also
Reference Time/Reference Date [TimeSequence]
Time Reference [TimeSequence]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4269
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Reference Time/Reference Date [TimeSequence]
For Time Reference > Relative you define a Reference Time. For Time Reference > Absolute you define
a Reference Date.
Remarks
Plant Simulation adds this value to the time column of the TimeSequence to offset the data you set there.
By changing the Reference Time/Date, you can shift the values in time without re-entering the data.
SimTalk
ReferenceDate [SimTalk] - Trigger
ReferenceTime [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
