Value [TimeSequence]
Type in a relative or an absolute path to the value that the TimeSequence is to record.
Remarks
When you specify an invalid path, the TimeSequence does not record any data. When you select Watch
mode, the path must reference a watchable value.
To check which attributes of an object are watchable, select the object and press F8. Watchable attributes
are marked with an asterisk (*) in the column Watchable in the window Show Attributes and Methods.
Example
I.building2.entrance.NumMU
frame.variable
ResWorking
SimTalk
Path [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Value [TimeSequence]
11-4272 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Mode [drop-down list] - TimeSequence
Select the mode with which the TimeSequence adds new time-value pairs to the columns of the table:
Watch or Sample.
Remarks
You can select one of these settings:
• Watch adds a new value each time when a watchable value changes.
The column Watchable in the window Show Attributes and Methods shows if an attribute is
watchable or not.
• Sample adds a new value periodically during the Interval that you specify, no matter if the value
actually changes or not.
SimTalk
